      "question": {
        ":question/id": "a103d3fe-7e8e-5e2a-bb52-c7e20925fab4",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Differentiate ${4}^{x}\\sin(x).$\n\n$(4^{x} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})'=$ {{field-1}} $+\\,(4^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=4^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(x)v(x))' &=u'(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot v'(x) \\\\ &=(4^{x})'\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(4^{x})\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})' \\\\ &=(4^{x} \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)})(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &\\quad +(4^{x})(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}) \\\\ &=4^{x} \\ln{\\left(4 \\right)} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\\\ &\\quad +(4^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
